// ===========================================================================
// OBESITY — LAYERED. The CONVENTION: layer MEASUREMENTS, merge DETERMINATIONS.
//
// ⭐ ONE OF THREE LEGITIMATE AUTHORING OPTIONS (operator, 2026-08-29), and the
// one we expect to establish as the convention. Assume an Obesity LIBRARY whose
// every layer some other library consumes.
//
// ⭐ TWO KINDS OF CONCEPT, AND THEY LAYER DIFFERENTLY.
//
// A MEASUREMENT is a thing you record repeatedly. You never add a "Height", you
// add a HEIGHT RECORD — so the history carries the code and IS the answer slot,
// and each Record above it is a NAMED SELECTION, derived and never answered.
// That is what the layer buys: `Most Recent Weight` and `Greatest Weight` are
// two selections over ONE history, and neither restates the code or the posrep.
//
// A DETERMINATION is a thing you conclude. It has ONE value and several ways to
// reach it — asserted, recorded externally, derived — and those are ARMS OF ONE
// CONCEPT, not separate concepts. `code is` + `source representation` +
// `definition is …, then most recent this` merges all three. Splitting them
// instead produces an answer slot nothing reads: MEASURED, an asserted obesity
// was accepted and ignored while the decision denied.
//
// ⚠ So the convention is NOT "layer everything". Layer a measurement, because a
// history genuinely has several selections. Do not layer a determination: it has
// one value, and separating its arms only removes the merge the language already
// performs.
// ===========================================================================
library "Obesity Coverage (Layered)".

terminology "Obese VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/obese`.
terminology "Clinical BMI VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/bmi`.
terminology "Height VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/height`.
terminology "Weight VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/weight`.

// ── MEASUREMENTS, layer 1 — the HISTORIES ──────────────────────────────────
// The answer slots for the raw measurements. Answering means adding a record,
// so an answer is in the history by construction.

concept "Height Records":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `height`.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Height VS".

concept "Weight Records":
- shape is RecordSet.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `weight`.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Weight VS".

// ── MEASUREMENTS, layer 2 — the NAMED SELECTIONS ───────────────────────────
// Each names ONE reduction of ONE history. Uncoded: a selection is not a thing
// you answer. ⭐ Two selections over `Weight Records` is the point of the layer.

concept "Most Recent Height":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- definition is most recent "Height Records".

concept "Most Recent Weight":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- definition is most recent "Weight Records".

concept "Greatest Weight":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- definition is highest "Weight Records".

// ── DETERMINATIONS — one concept, arms merged ──────────────────────────────
// NOT layered. Each has one value reached three ways, and `, then most recent
// this` reduces over the concept's OWN records — which is where the asserted
// arm (`code is`) and the recorded arm (`source representation`) both live. So
// the merge is the concept, and the concept is answerable.

// Derived from the measurement selections; also recordable and assertable.
concept "BMI":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `bmi`.
- definition is body mass index of "Most Recent Weight" and "Most Recent Height", then most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Clinical BMI VS".

// The coverage criterion. Asserted by a clinician, recorded as a Condition, or
// derived from BMI — whichever is newest wins.
concept "Obese":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `obese`.
- definition is "BMI" at least 30 'kg/m2', then most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is Condition.
  - coded from "Obese VS".
  - value projection is exists this.

activity "Approve Bariatric Surgery":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `APPROVED`.

activity "Deny Bariatric Surgery":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `NOT APPROVED`.

decision "Bariatric Surgery Coverage":
first:
- when "Obese" then recommend activity "Approve Bariatric Surgery".
- otherwise then recommend activity "Deny Bariatric Surgery".
